COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.spec.height_pixels IS 'The height dimension of the ad unit in pixels. Null for non-digital formats.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.spec.iab_standard_unit IS 'The IAB standard ad unit designation if this specification conforms to an IAB standard (e.g., ''Medium Rectangle'', ''Leaderboard'', ''Skyscraper'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.spec.max_animation_loops IS 'The maximum number of times an animated creative is allowed to loop. Null if unlimited or not applicable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.spec.max_duration_seconds IS 'The maximum duration for video or audio creatives in seconds. Null for non-time-based formats.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.spec.max_file_size_kb IS 'The maximum allowed file size for the creative asset in kilobytes (KB).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.spec.min_duration_seconds IS 'The minimum duration for video or audio creatives in seconds. Null for non-time-based formats.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.spec.notes IS 'Additional notes, guidelines, or special instructions for creative teams regarding this specification (e.g., platform-specific quirks, best practices, known issues).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.spec.platform IS 'The advertising platform or channel for which this specification applies (e.g., Google CM360, Meta, TikTok, LinkedIn, OOH Print, DOOH Digital, CTV, OTT). Code set: ref.platform.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.spec.platform_spec_version IS 'The version of the platform-specific specification this record is based on (e.g., ''Meta Q1 2024'', ''Google CM360 v3.2''). Used to track spec changes as platforms update requirements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.spec.resolution_dpi IS 'The required resolution for print or high-resolution digital creatives in dots per inch (DPI). Typically 300 DPI for print, 72 DPI for web.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.spec.safe_zone_pixels IS 'The safe zone margin in pixels where critical content (text, logos) must remain to avoid being cut off during display or printing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.spec.spec_code IS 'Unique business identifier code for the specification, used for system integration and asset validation workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.spec.spec_name IS 'Human-readable name for the creative specification (e.g., ''Facebook Feed Image Standard'', ''Google Display 300x250'', ''Instagram Story Video'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.spec.spec_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the creative specification (active, deprecated, draft, archived, pending approval, retired).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.spec.transparency_allowed IS 'Indicates whether the creative format supports transparency (alpha channel) in images (True) or requires opaque backgrounds (False).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.spec.video_codec IS 'The required video codec for video creatives (e.g., H.264, H.265, VP9). Null for non-video formats.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.spec.width_pixels IS 'The width dimension of the ad unit in pixels. Null for non-digital formats.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.spec.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.spec.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.spec.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.spec.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE creative.asset IS 'Core master entity representing a single creative asset in the Digital Asset Management system — including images, videos, audio files, copy documents, design files (PSD, AI, INDD), motion graphics, HTML5 rich media, and 3D/AR assets. Tracks asset type, format, file size, resolution, duration, codec, color profile, aspect ratio, DAM asset ID (Workfront DAM/Adobe AEM), version lineage, brand compliance status, rights clearance status, lifecycle stage (WIP, in-review, approved, archived, expired), expiry date, and descriptive metadata tags (subject, mood, channel, campaign theme). This is the SSOT for all creative asset metadata and taxonomy across the agency, supporting search, retrieval, reuse discovery, and rights monitoring.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.asset_id IS 'Unique identifier for the creative asset in the Digital Asset Management (DAM) system. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.advertiser_id IS 'FK to client.advertiser.advertiser_id — MUST-HAVE: Cannot determine asset ownership. Required for rights management, brand compliance, and client asset libraries. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.advertiser.advertiser_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.brand_id IS 'Reference to the client brand that owns or is represented by this asset. Enables brand-level asset organization and reporting. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.brand.brand_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.creative_brief_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.creative_brief. Business justification: A creative asset is produced in direct response to a creative brief — the brief defines the key message, tone, mandatories, deliverable formats, and brand direction that govern the asset. Adding creat';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.initiative_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.initiative. Business justification: Assets are deliverables within initiatives. Linking enables asset inventory management, reuse tracking across projects, ROI analysis, and portfolio reporting. Essential for digital asset management an';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.parent_asset_creative_asset_id IS 'Reference to the parent or original asset from which this version was derived. Establishes version lineage and asset family relationships.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.persona_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.persona. Business justification: Dynamic Creative Optimization (DCO) and personalization workflows require assets to be mapped to specific personas. Creative performance reporting by persona (e.g., ''which assets performed best for th LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.persona.persona_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.production_job_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.production_job. Business justification: A creative asset is the output artifact of a production job. Linking creative_asset to the production_job that produced it provides operational traceability — enabling job-level asset inventory, cost';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.segment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.segment. Business justification: Assets are optimized for specific audience segments; personalization and dynamic creative optimization require segment-level asset assignment to deliver relevant creative to each audience, core to mod LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.segment.segment_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.spec_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.spec. Business justification: Creative assets are produced to meet specific creative specifications (format, dimensions, file size, codec, etc.). This link tracks which spec an asset was produced to, supporting validation and comp';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Assets created by external vendors (stock media providers, production companies, freelance studios) require vendor attribution for rights management, usage tracking, invoice reconciliation, and qualit LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.task_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.task. Business justification: Assets are outputs of specific tasks. Linking enables granular effort tracking, resource utilization analysis, task completion validation, and productivity measurement. Essential for time tracking and';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.work_package_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.work_package. Business justification: Creative assets are produced within specific work packages (e.g., ''Digital Asset Production WP''). Direct work_package_id on creative_asset enables work-package-level asset inventory and cost reporting';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.approved_timestamp IS 'Date and time when the asset was approved for use. Establishes the point at which the asset became available for trafficking and deployment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.archived_timestamp IS 'Date and time when the asset was archived or retired from active use. Supports lifecycle management and storage optimization.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.aspect_ratio IS 'Proportional relationship between width and height (e.g., 16:9, 4:3, 1:1, 9:16). Determines display format and channel suitability.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.asset_name IS 'Human-readable name or title of the creative asset. Primary label used for search and identification.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.asset_type IS 'High-level classification of the creative asset format. Determines handling, rendering, and distribution workflows. Code set: ref.asset_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.brand_compliance_status IS 'Indicates whether the asset adheres to brand guidelines and standards. Critical for brand integrity and legal risk management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.campaign_theme IS 'Overarching creative theme or concept associated with the asset (e.g., Summer Sale, Back to School, Holiday 2024). Links asset to strategic messaging.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.channel_suitability IS 'Comma-separated list of media channels for which this asset is optimized or approved (e.g., TV, Digital, OOH, Social, CTV). Guides media planning and trafficking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.codec IS 'Video or audio codec used for encoding (e.g., H.264, H.265, AAC, MP3). Critical for playback compatibility and quality.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.color_profile IS 'Color space or profile used in the asset (e.g., sRGB, Adobe RGB, CMYK). Ensures color accuracy across media and devices.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.copyright_holder IS 'Name of the individual or organization that holds copyright to the asset. Critical for legal compliance and rights management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.creative_asset_description IS 'Free-text description of the asset content, purpose, and usage notes. Provides context for search, reuse, and creative briefing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.dam_asset_ref IS 'External unique identifier from the source DAM system (Workfront DAM or Adobe AEM). Used for cross-system reconciliation and asset retrieval.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.duration_seconds IS 'Length of the asset in seconds. Applicable to video, audio, and motion graphics assets.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.file_format IS 'Specific file format or extension of the asset (e.g., PSD, AI, INDD, MP4, PNG, JPG, HTML5). Critical for compatibility and production workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.file_size_bytes IS 'Size of the asset file in bytes. Used for storage management, bandwidth planning, and delivery optimization.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.file_storage_path IS 'Full path or URI to the asset file in the storage system (cloud storage, DAM repository, CDN). Used for retrieval and delivery.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.geographic_market IS 'Target geographic market or region for which the asset was created (e.g., USA, GBR, CAN). Supports regional campaign management and compliance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.is_master_asset IS 'Flag indicating whether this asset is the master or source-of-truth version from which other versions are derived. True for master assets, false for derivatives.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.language_code IS 'ISO 639-1 two-letter language code indicating the primary language of the asset (e.g., EN, ES, FR). Critical for localization and regional targeting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.license_type IS 'Type of license under which the asset is used (e.g., royalty-free, rights-managed, exclusive, non-exclusive). Governs usage terms and restrictions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.lifecycle_stage IS 'Current stage in the creative asset lifecycle. Governs access, usage rights, and workflow routing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.mood_tags IS 'Comma-separated keywords describing the emotional tone or mood of the asset (e.g., energetic, calm, humorous, inspirational). Aids in creative selection and reuse.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.resolution IS 'Pixel dimensions or resolution of the asset (e.g., 1920x1080, 300 DPI). Applicable to images and videos.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.rights_clearance_status IS 'Status of legal rights and usage permissions for the asset (talent, music, stock imagery, etc.). Determines where and how the asset can be used.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.rights_expiry_date IS 'Date when usage rights for the asset expire. After this date, the asset may no longer be legally used without renewal.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.subject_tags IS 'Comma-separated descriptive keywords describing the subject matter or content of the asset (e.g., product, lifestyle, testimonial). Supports search and discovery.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.thumbnail_url IS 'URL to a thumbnail or preview image of the asset. Enables quick visual identification in DAM interfaces and reporting tools.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.usage_count IS 'Number of times this asset has been used in campaigns, ads, or other placements. Indicates asset popularity and reuse value.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.version_number IS 'Version identifier for the asset (e.g., v1.0, v2.3, final). Tracks iteration and revision history.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE creative.asset_version IS 'Tracks the full version history of a creative asset — capturing each iteration produced during the creative development lifecycle. Records version number, version label (e.g., v1, v2_client_feedback), file reference, change summary, author, Adobe CC document version ID, Workfront proof version ID, and promotion status (draft, in-review, approved, superseded). Enables rollback, audit, and compliance traceability for all creative deliverables.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.asset_version_id IS 'Unique identifier for the asset version record. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.asset_id IS 'Reference to the parent creative asset for which this version was created.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.creative_deliverable_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.creative_deliverable. Business justification: Asset versions represent iterative development states of deliverables. Production tracking requires linking each version to its parent deliverable to manage revision history, track which version was a';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.deliverable_tracker_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.deliverable_tracker. Business justification: Specific asset versions are submitted as deliverables and tracked in deliverable_tracker (which stores file_reference and version_number as plain text). A proper FK normalizes this and enables version';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.production_job_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.production_job. Business justification: Each asset version is produced within the context of a specific production job — revisions, re-renders, and format adaptations are all tracked as versions tied to the job that commissioned them. Addin';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.spec_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.spec. Business justification: Each asset version should track which creative specification it conforms to. As assets are revised through the version history, they may be adjusted to meet different specs or updated spec versions. T';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.task_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.task. Business justification: In advertising production, each asset version is created during a specific revision or QA task. Linking asset_version to task enables task-level version history reporting and effort-to-version traceab';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.adobe_cc_document_version_ref IS 'External version identifier from Adobe Creative Cloud system. Enables traceability to source Adobe application (Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign, Premiere Pro).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.approval_timestamp IS 'Date and time when this version received formal approval. Null if not yet approved.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.approved_by_name IS 'Name of the individual who approved this version for promotion or final delivery. Null if not yet approved.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.archive_timestamp IS 'Date and time when this version was archived. Null if not yet archived.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.brand_compliance_status IS 'Indicates whether this version adheres to brand guidelines and standards. Used for brand governance and quality control.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.change_summary IS 'Brief description of changes made in this version compared to the previous iteration. Captures rationale for the revision.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.checksum_hash IS 'Cryptographic hash (e.g., MD5, SHA-256) of the file for integrity verification and duplicate detection.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.color_profile IS 'Color space or profile used in this version (e.g., sRGB, Adobe RGB, CMYK). Critical for print and digital color accuracy.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.compliance_check_timestamp IS 'Date and time when brand compliance review was last performed on this version. Null if not yet reviewed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.duration_seconds IS 'Duration of video or audio creative in seconds. Null for static assets.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.file_format IS 'File format or extension of this version (e.g., PSD, AI, INDD, PDF, JPG, PNG, MP4, MOV). Indicates the Adobe Creative Cloud or export format. Code set: ref.file_format.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.file_name IS 'Original file name of this version as stored in the system.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.file_path IS 'Storage location or URI reference to the physical file for this version in the Digital Asset Management (DAM) system or cloud storage.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.file_size_bytes IS 'Size of the version file in bytes. Used for storage management and delivery optimization.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.height_pixels IS 'Height dimension of the creative asset in pixels. Applicable to image and video formats.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.is_archived IS 'Indicates whether this version has been archived and moved to long-term storage. True if archived, False if active.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.is_promoted IS 'Indicates whether this version has been promoted to production or final delivery status. True if promoted, False otherwise.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.promotion_timestamp IS 'Date and time when this version was promoted to production or approved for final delivery. Null if not yet promoted.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.rejection_reason IS 'Explanation or rationale for rejection if this version was not approved. Null if approved or pending.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.resolution_dpi IS 'Resolution of the asset in dots per inch. Typically 72 for digital, 300+ for print. Null for video assets.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.version_label IS 'Human-readable version label or tag (e.g., v1, v2_client_feedback, v3_final, draft_A). Used for identification and communication.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.version_number IS 'Sequential numeric version number indicating the iteration sequence (1, 2, 3, etc.).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.version_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of this version. Tracks progression through creative approval workflow.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.width_pixels IS 'Width dimension of the creative asset in pixels. Applicable to image and video formats.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.workfront_proof_version_ref IS 'External proof version identifier from Workfront proofing system. Links to approval and feedback workflow.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.asset_version.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE creative.creative_deliverable IS 'Represents a specific creative deliverable committed to a client or campaign — a named output (e.g., ''30s TV spot :30'', ''MPU 300x250 HTML5 banner'', ''Full-page print ad'') with defined format, channel, quantity, and delivery deadline. Links the creative brief requirement to the production job and final approved asset. Tracks deliverable status (not-started, in-production, delivered, accepted) and client acceptance sign-off. Serves as the contractual unit of creative output.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.creative_deliverable_id IS 'Unique identifier for the creative deliverable. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.ad_format_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.ad_format. Business justification: Creative deliverables are produced for specific ad formats defined in the media plan. Linking deliverables to the media ad_format taxonomy enables trafficking teams to validate format compliance, supp LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.ad_format.ad_format_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the advertiser client for whom this deliverable is being produced. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.advertiser.advertiser_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.asset_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.asset. Business justification: A deliverable is fulfilled by a creative asset (the actual digital file in the DAM). The creative_deliverable table currently has dam_asset_id as a STRING, which should be normalized to a proper FK to';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: Creative deliverables are brand-specific assets. Brand compliance status tracking, brand-level delivery reporting, and brand guideline adherence checks on deliverables all require a direct brand FK. c LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.brand.brand_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the campaign this deliverable supports. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.contract_deliverable_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_deliverable. Business justification: Contract deliverables define what must be produced per agreement; creative_deliverable tracks actual creative execution. Linking these enables acceptance tracking, milestone completion validation, bil LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_deliverable.contract_deliverable_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.contract_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_insertion_order. Business justification: Creative deliverables fulfill specific contract insertion orders — the IO specifies placement, format, and flight that the deliverable must satisfy for trafficking. Named process: ''deliverable fulfill LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_insertion_order.contract_insertion_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Deliverables are produced by specific departments/studios tracked as cost centers. Enables cost allocation, departmental utilization reporting, and chargeback accounting for deliverable production cos LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.creative_brief_id IS 'Reference to the creative brief that defines the requirements for this deliverable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.deliverable_tracker_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.deliverable_tracker. Business justification: The creative_deliverable (creative domain record) must reconcile with the deliverable_tracker (project domain record) for unified delivery status reporting. Advertising agencies track deliverables in';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.initiative_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.initiative. Business justification: Deliverables are outputs of initiatives. Linking enables scope validation, milestone tracking, client reporting, and deliverable inventory management across the initiative lifecycle. Critical for proj';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.media_placement_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.media_placement. Business justification: Creative deliverables are produced for specific media placements. Trafficking teams must know which deliverable is assigned to which placement to execute ad serving. This placement-to-deliverable assi LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.media_placement.media_placement_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.milestone_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.milestone. Business justification: Deliverables are tied to contractual milestones. Linking enables billing trigger validation, client acceptance tracking, payment release management, and SOW compliance verification. Essential for reve';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.persona_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.persona. Business justification: Persona-based creative strategy requires deliverables to be assigned to specific personas (e.g., ''produce a 30s video for the Urban Millennial persona''). Persona-level deliverable tracking drives pers LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.persona.persona_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.plan_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.plan. Business justification: Deliverables are produced to fulfill media plan requirements. Creative teams need to know which plan drives each deliverable to ensure formats, specs, and deadlines align with media flight dates and c LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.plan.plan_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.production_job_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.production_job. Business justification: A creative deliverable is the output produced by a production job. This is a direct operational relationship: the production job is the unit of work that creates the deliverable. Cardinality: N:1 (one';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.project_budget_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.project_budget. Business justification: Deliverables have budget allocations. Linking enables cost-to-deliver tracking, profitability analysis, budget forecasting, and financial reporting. Critical for project financial management and prici';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.rate_card_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.rate_card_line. Business justification: Creative deliverables are billed at rates defined by contract rate card lines (e.g., per-asset production fee, per-format creative rate). Linking deliverable to rate_card_line enables accurate billing LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.rate_card_line.rate_card_line_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.segment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.segment. Business justification: Deliverables are tailored to audience segments; trafficking workflows and media plan execution require segment-level creative mapping to ensure correct creative serves to each audience, essential for LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.segment.segment_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.sla_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sla. Business justification: Creative deliverables are subject to contracted SLA terms governing turnaround times, revision cycles, and delivery standards. Agencies track SLA compliance per deliverable for performance reporting a LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sla.sla_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: Creative deliverables fulfill contractual obligations defined in SOWs. Tracking this link enables acceptance criteria validation, milestone-based invoicing, client sign-off workflows, and ensures deli LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sow.sow_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.spec_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.spec. Business justification: Deliverables must conform to creative specifications (platform requirements, format constraints, technical specs). The creative_deliverable table has format_specification as a STRING, which should be';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Deliverables produced by external vendors need vendor tracking for invoice reconciliation, quality management, SLA monitoring, and vendor performance evaluation. Essential for production operations an LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.task_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.task. Business justification: Creative deliverables are produced by specific project tasks (e.g., ''Copywriting Task'', ''Design Task''). Linking creative_deliverable to task enables task-level deliverable attribution, effort-to-deliv';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.work_package_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.work_package. Business justification: Deliverables map to specific work packages in WBS. Linking enables granular schedule tracking, resource allocation, earned value management, and deliverable-level progress reporting. Essential for pro';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.accepted_date IS 'Date when the client formally accepted the deliverable and signed off on completion.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.actual_cost IS 'Actual total production cost incurred for this deliverable, used for financial reconciliation and profitability analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.actual_hours IS 'Actual number of labor hours spent producing this deliverable, tracked for billing and performance analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.assigned_copywriter IS 'Name of the copywriter assigned to develop copy and messaging for this deliverable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.assigned_creative_team IS 'Name or identifier of the creative team or studio responsible for producing this deliverable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.brand_compliance_status IS 'Indicates whether the deliverable meets brand guideline requirements and has passed brand compliance review.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.channel IS 'Media channel where the deliverable will be deployed. Code set: ref.channel.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for cost and billing amounts (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.deliverable_code IS 'Unique business identifier or tracking code for the deliverable used across systems (e.g., ''SUMR-2024-TV-30S-001'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.deliverable_name IS 'Human-readable name of the creative deliverable (e.g., ''30s TV Spot - Summer Campaign'', ''MPU 300x250 HTML5 Banner'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.deliverable_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the creative deliverable in the production and approval workflow. Code set: ref.deliverable_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.deliverable_type IS 'Category of creative deliverable based on media format and channel. Code set: ref.deliverable_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.delivered_date IS 'Date when the deliverable was delivered to the client or uploaded to the delivery platform.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.delivery_method IS 'Method by which the deliverable was or will be delivered to the client or trafficking system.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.dimensions IS 'Physical or pixel dimensions of the deliverable (e.g., ''300x250'', ''1920x1080'', ''8.5x11 inches'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.due_date IS 'Contractual deadline by which the deliverable must be completed and delivered to the client.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.duration_seconds IS 'Duration of the creative deliverable in seconds, applicable to video and audio formats (e.g., 15, 30, 60).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.estimated_cost IS 'Estimated total production cost for this deliverable including labor, materials, and third-party services.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.estimated_hours IS 'Estimated number of labor hours required to complete this deliverable, used for resource planning and costing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.file_format IS 'File format of the final deliverable asset (e.g., MP4, HTML5, PDF, JPEG). Code set: ref.file_format.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.file_size_mb IS 'Size of the final deliverable file in megabytes, used for storage planning and delivery validation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.legal_approval_required IS 'Flag indicating whether this deliverable requires legal review and approval before delivery (e.g., for claims, disclaimers, regulatory compliance).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.legal_approval_status IS 'Current status of legal review and approval for this deliverable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.notes IS 'Free-text field for additional notes, special instructions, or context about the deliverable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.priority IS 'Business priority level assigned to this deliverable for resource allocation and scheduling.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.production_start_date IS 'Date when production work on this deliverable began.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.quantity_required IS 'Number of units or versions of this deliverable required (e.g., 3 language versions, 5 size variations).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.requested_date IS 'Date when the deliverable was originally requested by the client or account team.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.revision_count IS 'Number of revision cycles this deliverable has undergone since initial submission.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.version_number IS 'Version identifier for the deliverable to track iterations and revisions (e.g., ''v1.0'', ''v2.3'', ''Final'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.creative_deliverable.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE creative.production_job IS 'Operational record representing a discrete creative production job — the unit of work assigned to an internal studio team, freelancer, or external production vendor to produce one or more creative deliverables. Tracks job type (print, digital, video, audio, OOH, DOOH, CTV, social, experiential), job status (briefed, in-production, internal-review, QA, client-review, delivered), assigned studio or production house, estimated and actual production hours, cost estimate vs actual cost, delivery deadline, and priority level. Links to creative brief requirements and spawns creative assets upon completion. Sourced from Workfront project tasks and integrates with SAP PS for cost tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.production_job_id IS 'Unique identifier for the production job. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: Production jobs are executed for a specific brand. Brand-level production cost reporting, brand compliance requirement enforcement, and brand-scoped production capacity planning all require this direc LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.brand.brand_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the campaign this production job supports. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.concept_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.concept. Business justification: Production jobs execute approved concepts. Once a concept is approved, production jobs are created to produce the creative deliverables. This direct link allows tracking which concept a production job';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Production jobs are core cost-tracking units in agency operations. Jobs are allocated to cost centers (studio, creative department) for labor cost accounting, overhead allocation, and departmental P&L LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.creative_brief_id IS 'Reference to the creative brief that initiated this production job.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.delivery_project_milestone_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.milestone. Business justification: Production job delivery deadlines align with contractual project milestones (e.g., ''Final Delivery'' milestone that triggers client billing). Role-prefix ''delivery_'' distinguishes this from other poten';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.gl_account_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.gl_account. Business justification: Production job costs post directly to GL accounts in agency accounting (SAP/NetSuite). production_job already has sap_wbs_element indicating ERP integration; GL account assignment is required for cost LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.gl_account.gl_account_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.plan_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.plan. Business justification: Production jobs are initiated to create deliverables for media plans. Studios need plan context for format specifications, channel requirements, flight deadlines, and ensuring creative is ready before LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.plan.plan_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.primary_production_initiative_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.initiative. Business justification: Production jobs are work execution units within initiatives. Linking enables project portfolio reporting, resource planning across initiatives, budget roll-ups, and timeline tracking. Essential for ag';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.project_budget_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.project_budget. Business justification: Production jobs consume project budgets. Linking enables cost tracking, variance analysis, budget utilization reporting, and profitability analysis. Essential for financial management and project cont';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.sla_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sla. Business justification: Production jobs are subject to contracted SLA commitments covering delivery timelines and revision turnaround. Agencies track whether production jobs meet contracted SLA terms for performance reportin LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sla.sla_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: Production jobs are delivered under SOW terms that define deliverables, timelines, and pricing. Agencies track which SOW governs each job for accurate billing, resource allocation, and contract compli LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sow.sow_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Production jobs are frequently outsourced to external studios, post-production facilities, VFX houses, and freelance production companies. Critical for vendor billing reconciliation, quality managemen LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.task_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.task. Business justification: Production jobs in advertising are executed through specific project tasks (e.g., ''Studio Production Task''). Linking production_job to task enables time-entry reconciliation against production jobs an';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.vendor_rate_card_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.vendor_rate_card. Business justification: Production cost management: when a supplier is engaged for a production job, the agreed vendor rate card governs billing, cost estimation, and reconciliation. Production managers and finance teams nee LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.vendor_rate_card.vendor_rate_card_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.work_package_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.work_package. Business justification: Production jobs are work packages in project plans. Linking enables task-level tracking, capacity planning, WBS-based reporting, and resource utilization analysis. Critical for studio operations manag';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.actual_cost IS 'Actual total cost incurred for this production job, reconciled from time tracking, vendor invoices, and expense reports.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.actual_hours IS 'Actual total production hours spent on this job, tracked for cost reconciliation and future estimation accuracy.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.assigned_studio IS 'Name of the internal studio team, freelancer, or external production vendor assigned to execute this job.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.brand_compliance_required IS 'Indicates whether this production job requires formal brand guideline compliance review and approval.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.brand_compliance_status IS 'Status of brand compliance review for this job. Values: not-required (compliance not needed), pending (review in progress), passed (compliant), failed (non-compliant), waived (compliance waived by client).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.client_approval_date IS 'Date when the client formally approved the final creative deliverables for this job.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.client_feedback IS 'Feedback and comments received from the client during review cycles, captured for revision guidance and future reference.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for all monetary amounts in this production job (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.deliverable_count IS 'Total number of distinct creative assets or deliverables produced as part of this production job.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.delivery_deadline IS 'Target date by which final creative assets must be delivered to the client or campaign team.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.estimated_cost IS 'Estimated total cost to complete this production job, including labor, vendor fees, and production expenses.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.estimated_hours IS 'Estimated total production hours required to complete this job, used for resource planning and capacity management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.final_delivery_date IS 'Date when final approved creative assets were delivered to the client or campaign team.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.format_specifications IS 'Technical format requirements for the deliverables (e.g., dimensions, file types, color space, resolution, duration). Free-text field capturing brief requirements from the creative brief.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.internal_notes IS 'Internal notes and comments from the production team, not shared with the client. May include production challenges, resource constraints, or process observations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.is_billable IS 'Indicates whether this production job is billable to the client or is internal/non-billable work.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.job_description IS 'Detailed description of the production job scope, objectives, and deliverables as defined in the creative brief or project plan.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.job_name IS 'Human-readable name or title of the production job, typically describing the deliverable or campaign element.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.job_number IS 'Externally-known unique job number assigned by the production management system (e.g., Workfront). Format typically includes prefix and sequential number.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.job_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the production job. Values: briefed (job briefed, not started), in-production (active production work), internal-review (internal creative review), qa (quality assurance check), client-review (submitted to client), revisions (rework requested), approved (client approved), delivered (final assets delivered), cancelled (job cancelled). Code set: ref.job_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.job_type IS 'Category of creative production work. Values: print (print advertising), digital (digital display/banner), video (video production), audio (radio/podcast), ooh (Out-of-Home static), dooh (Digital Out-of-Home), ctv (Connected TV), social (social media creative), experiential (event/activation), motion-graphics (animation/motion design). Code set: ref.job_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.legal_review_required IS 'Indicates whether this production job requires legal or regulatory compliance review (e.g., for claims, disclosures, or regulated industries).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.legal_review_status IS 'Status of legal compliance review for this job. Values: not-required (legal review not needed), pending (review in progress), approved (legally compliant), rejected (non-compliant), conditional (approved with modifications).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.priority_level IS 'Business priority assigned to this production job, determining resource allocation and scheduling urgency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.production_completion_date IS 'Date when production work was completed and job moved to review or delivery status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.production_start_date IS 'Date when active production work began on this job.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.revision_count IS 'Total number of revision rounds requested by internal reviewers or client during the production lifecycle.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.sap_wbs_element IS 'SAP Project Systems WBS element code used for cost tracking and financial reconciliation of this production job.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.production_job.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_by.';

COMMENT ON TABLE creative.proof IS 'Captures each formal proofing round submitted for client or internal review via Workfront Proofing. Records proof type (concept, copy, layout, final art, legal, accessibility), proof stage (internal, client round 1/2/3, final), reviewer assignments, due date, submission timestamp, overall proof decision (approved, approved-with-changes, rejected), and decision timestamp. Distinct from asset_version in that a proof is a formal review event with stakeholder decisions and SLA tracking, not merely a file iteration. Supports agency SLA compliance reporting on review turnaround times.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.proof_id IS 'Unique identifier for the proof record. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.asset_version_id IS 'Reference to the specific asset version being proofed in this review cycle.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the campaign this proof is associated with, enabling campaign-level proof tracking and SLA reporting. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.creative_deliverable_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.creative_deliverable. Business justification: A proof is submitted to validate a specific creative deliverable — the proof round is the formal approval mechanism for a named deliverable output. While proof already links to asset_version (the spec';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.deliverable_tracker_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.deliverable_tracker. Business justification: A proof is the review/approval mechanism for a tracked deliverable. Linking proof to deliverable_tracker enables end-to-end delivery and approval workflow reporting — advertising agencies need to reco';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.initiative_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.initiative. Business justification: Proofs are approval artifacts within initiatives. Linking enables workflow tracking, approval cycle analysis, timeline management, and client satisfaction measurement at the initiative level. Essentia';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.milestone_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.milestone. Business justification: Proofs are approval gates at milestones. Linking enables contractual compliance, payment release validation, client sign-off tracking, and milestone achievement verification. Critical for contract man';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.production_job_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.production_job. Business justification: Proofs are submitted during production jobs as part of the creative review workflow. This link provides operational context: which production job is this proof part of? Supports workflow tracking, SLA';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.sla_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sla. Business justification: Proof review cycles are governed by contracted SLA turnaround commitments. proof.sla_met_flag and sla_target_hours are denormalized SLA data; linking to the governing SLA record enables breach reporti LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sla.sla_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Proofing platforms (Workfront Proof, Ziflow, Aproove) are often external SaaS vendors. Required for vendor contract management, platform cost allocation, and tech stack governance in creative operatio LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.task_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.task. Business justification: Proofs are approval tasks in project schedules. Linking enables dependency management, timeline tracking, task completion validation, and approval workflow automation. Critical for schedule management';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.work_package_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.work_package. Business justification: Proofs are approval milestones within work packages. Linking enables critical path management, approval cycle tracking, and schedule impact analysis. Essential for timeline management and client coord';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.approval_count IS 'Number of reviewers who approved the proof (either approved or approved with changes). Used for consensus tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.automated_check_flag IS 'Indicates whether automated compliance checks (legal, accessibility, brand guidelines) were run on this proof. True = automated checks performed, False = manual review only.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.automated_check_result IS 'Result of automated compliance checks if performed. Pass = all checks passed, Fail = critical issues found, Warning = minor issues flagged, Not Applicable = no automated checks run.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.comment_count IS 'Total number of comments and annotations submitted by all reviewers on this proof. Indicator of feedback volume and creative iteration intensity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.decision_timestamp IS 'Date and time when the overall proof decision was finalized. Used as the end point for SLA turnaround time calculations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.due_date IS 'Target date by which all reviewers must complete their review and provide decisions. Used for SLA compliance tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.escalation_flag IS 'Indicates whether this proof was escalated to senior stakeholders due to missed SLA, critical feedback, or client dissatisfaction. True = escalated, False = normal workflow.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.escalation_reason IS 'Free-text explanation of why the proof was escalated (e.g., ''Client rejected 3 consecutive rounds'', ''SLA missed by 48 hours'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.instructions IS 'Free-text instructions or context provided to reviewers about what to focus on in this proof (e.g., ''Please review headline copy for brand voice compliance'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.overall_decision IS 'Consolidated decision outcome across all assigned reviewers. Approved = all reviewers approved, Approved with Changes = approved but revisions requested, Rejected = requires major rework, Pending = awaiting reviewer decisions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.proof_name IS 'Descriptive name of the proof, typically derived from the asset name and proof round (e.g., ''Q1 Campaign Hero Banner - Client Round 2'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.proof_number IS 'Human-readable business identifier for the proof, typically auto-generated in format PRF-YYYYMMDD or similar.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.proof_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the proof. Draft = being prepared, Submitted = sent to reviewers, In Review = active review in progress, Approved = accepted as-is, Approved with Changes = accepted with minor revisions, Rejected = requires major rework, Cancelled = proof withdrawn. Code set: ref.proof_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.proof_type IS 'Type of proof being submitted for review. Concept = early ideation, Copy = text/messaging review, Layout = design structure, Final Art = production-ready creative, Legal = regulatory compliance review, Accessibility = WCAG/ADA compliance, Brand Compliance = brand guideline adherence. Code set: ref.proof_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.rejection_count IS 'Number of reviewers who rejected the proof. Used for quality control and creative iteration analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.reviewer_count IS 'Total number of reviewers assigned to this proof. Used for workload and stakeholder engagement analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.round_number IS 'Sequential round number for this proof within the asset version lifecycle (1 = first proof, 2 = second proof after revisions, etc.).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.sla_met_flag IS 'Boolean indicator of whether the proof review was completed within the SLA target hours. True = SLA met, False = SLA missed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.stage IS 'Stage of the proofing workflow. Internal = agency-only review, Client Round 1/2/3 = sequential client review cycles, Final = final approval before production.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.submission_timestamp IS 'Date and time when the proof was formally submitted to reviewers. Used as the start point for SLA turnaround time calculations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.turnaround_time_hours IS 'Calculated elapsed time in hours between submission_timestamp and decision_timestamp. Key metric for agency SLA compliance reporting on review cycle speed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.url IS 'Direct URL link to the proof in the Workfront Proofing system for reviewer access and audit trail.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN creative.proof.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE project.assignment IS 'Operational record linking a specific worker or team member to a task or work package within a project. Captures assignee worker reference, task or work package reference, assignment role (lead, contributor, reviewer, approver), planned hours, actual hours logged, assignment start date, assignment end date, allocation percentage, billable flag, billing rate applied, assignment status (active, completed, reassigned), and reassignment reason. Bridges project execution with talent workforce data and enables utilization tracking at the task level.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.assignment_id IS 'Unique identifier for the assignment record. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.contract_rate_card_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_rate_card. Business justification: project_assignment has billing_rate and cost_rate that must be validated against the contracted rate card header. In advertising agencies, assignment billing rates are governed by client-negotiated ra LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_rate_card.contract_rate_card_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.initiative_id IS 'Reference to the parent project to which this assignment belongs.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.rate_card_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.rate_card_line. Business justification: Individual assignments in advertising agencies are priced at specific rate card line items (e.g., Senior Art Director at $X/hr per the SOW rate card). rate_card_line has role_title, seniority_level, u LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.rate_card_line.rate_card_line_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.reassigned_from_project_assignment_id IS 'Self-referencing FK on project_assignment (reassigned_from_project_assignment_id)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.resource_plan_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.resource_plan. Business justification: project_assignment (actual staffing) fulfills project_resource_plan (demand plan). Linking the assignment back to the resource plan it was created to fulfill closes the demand-to-actuals loop: agencie';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: Resource assignments are scoped to SOWs. Agencies track which SOW funds each assignment for cost allocation, billing rate application, and ensuring resource deployment aligns with contractual scope an LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sow.sow_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.task_id IS 'Reference to the specific task or work package within the project that this assignment addresses.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.work_package_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.work_package. Business justification: The product description explicitly states project_assignment links ''a specific worker or team member to a task or work package.'' The existing FK covers task_id but work_package_id is missing. Some ass';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.actual_hours IS 'The actual number of hours logged by the worker against the assigned task. Used for utilization tracking and billing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.allocation_percentage IS 'The percentage of the worker''s capacity allocated to this assignment, expressed as a decimal (e.g., 50.00 for 50% allocation).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.assigned_timestamp IS 'The date and time when the assignment was created or assigned to the worker.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.assignment_role IS 'The role or capacity in which the worker is assigned to the task (e.g., lead, contributor, reviewer, approver, observer, consultant).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.assignment_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the assignment indicating whether it is active, completed, reassigned, on hold, or cancelled.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.billable_flag IS 'Indicates whether the hours worked on this assignment are billable to the client (True) or non-billable (False).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.billing_rate IS 'The hourly billing rate applied to this assignment for client invoicing purposes. Confidential business data.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.completed_timestamp IS 'The date and time when the assignment was marked as completed by the worker or project manager.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.cost_rate IS 'The internal cost rate per hour for the worker on this assignment, used for profitability analysis. Confidential business data.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for billing and cost rates (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.end_date IS 'The date on which the worker is scheduled to complete work on the assigned task.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.notes IS 'Additional notes or instructions related to the assignment, such as special requirements or context for the worker.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.overtime_eligible_flag IS 'Indicates whether the worker is eligible for overtime compensation on this assignment (True) or not (False).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.planned_hours IS 'The estimated number of hours allocated for the worker to complete the assigned task.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.priority IS 'The priority level of this assignment relative to other assignments for the worker (critical, high, medium, low).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.reassigned_timestamp IS 'The date and time when the assignment was reassigned to a different worker, if applicable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.reassignment_reason IS 'Free-text explanation for why the assignment was reassigned to a different worker, if applicable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.skill_required IS 'The primary skill or competency required for this assignment (e.g., copywriting, art direction, media planning, data analysis).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.start_date IS 'The date on which the worker is scheduled to begin work on the assigned task.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.utilization_category IS 'Classification of the assignment for workforce utilization reporting (e.g., client billable, internal project, training, administrative, bench).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.work_location IS 'Indicates whether the assignment is to be performed on-site at the client or agency location, remotely, or in a hybrid arrangement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.assignment.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE project.deliverable_tracker IS 'Operational tracking record for each project deliverable — monitoring production progress from brief through final delivery. Captures deliverable name, deliverable type (creative asset, media plan, strategy deck, report, campaign setup, trafficking sheet, etc.), associated work package, planned delivery date, actual delivery date, delivery status (not started, in production, in review, approved, delivered, rejected), review round count, client approval status, format specifications, file reference, and delivery channel (email, portal, FTP, DAM). Distinct from contract.deliverable (contractual commitment) — this is the operational production tracking record.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.deliverable_tracker_id IS 'Unique identifier for the deliverable tracking record. Primary key for operational tracking of project deliverables from brief through final delivery.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the campaign this deliverable supports, if applicable. Links deliverable to the broader campaign execution. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.contract_deliverable_id IS 'Reference to the contractual deliverable commitment in the Statement of Work (SOW) or Insertion Order (IO). Links operational tracking to contractual obligation. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_deliverable.contract_deliverable_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.initiative_id IS 'Reference to the parent project under which this deliverable is being produced.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.milestone_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.milestone. Business justification: Deliverables are reviewed and approved at milestone gates (project_milestone has is_billing_trigger and is_contractual_gate flags). Linking deliverable_tracker to project_milestone enables the system';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.plan_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.plan. Business justification: Media plans are contractual deliverables tracked through project delivery workflows. Required for client approval gates, billing triggers tied to plan delivery, and SOW compliance verification in agen LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.plan.plan_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.project_brief_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.project_brief. Business justification: Deliverables are defined and scoped in the project_brief (key_deliverables, scope_description, success_criteria). Linking deliverable_tracker to project_brief provides direct traceability from the bri';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.revision_of_deliverable_tracker_id IS 'Self-referencing FK on deliverable_tracker (revision_of_deliverable_tracker_id)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Deliverables in advertising (video assets, display creatives, media placements) are produced by specific vendors. Linking supplier_id to deliverable_tracker enables vendor-level delivery performance r LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.task_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.task. Business justification: A deliverable is produced by executing specific tasks. deliverable_tracker already links to work_package_id (the container) but lacks a direct link to the specific task that produces the deliverable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.trafficking_instruction_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.trafficking_instruction. Business justification: Trafficking instructions are formal deliverables in ad agency project management — they must be authored, reviewed, approved, and sent to ad servers. Project teams track each instruction as a delivera LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.trafficking_instruction.trafficking_instruction_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.work_package_id IS 'Reference to the work package or work breakdown structure element that this deliverable belongs to.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.actual_delivery_date IS 'Actual date on which the deliverable was delivered. Used to measure on-time delivery performance and project execution accuracy.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.actual_hours IS 'Actual effort in hours logged against this deliverable. Used to measure estimation accuracy and project profitability.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.approved_timestamp IS 'Timestamp when the deliverable received final client approval. Marks formal acceptance and completion of the deliverable lifecycle.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.client_approval_status IS 'Current approval state from the client perspective. Indicates whether the client has formally accepted the deliverable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.compliance_check_status IS 'Status of regulatory and brand compliance review. Ensures deliverable meets legal, regulatory, and brand guideline requirements before delivery.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.deliverable_name IS 'Business name or title of the deliverable being tracked (e.g., ''Q4 Brand Campaign Video'', ''Media Plan Deck'', ''Trafficking Sheet'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.deliverable_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the deliverable in the production workflow. Tracks progression from initiation through final delivery. Code set: ref.deliverable_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.deliverable_type IS 'Classification of the deliverable by format and purpose. Distinguishes creative assets from strategic documents, operational setup files, and reporting outputs. Code set: ref.deliverable_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.delivered_timestamp IS 'Precise timestamp when the deliverable was marked as delivered. Provides exact delivery time for Service Level Agreement (SLA) measurement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.delivery_channel IS 'Method or platform through which the deliverable was or will be transmitted to the recipient (e.g., email, client portal, FTP, DAM system). Code set: ref.delivery_channel.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.delivery_notes IS 'Free-text notes accompanying the deliverable delivery. May include usage instructions, context, or special handling requirements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.estimated_hours IS 'Planned effort in hours required to complete this deliverable. Used for resource planning and capacity management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.file_reference IS 'File path, URL, or Digital Asset Management (DAM) system reference pointing to the deliverable asset location.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.format_specification IS 'Technical format requirements for the deliverable (e.g., ''MP4 1920x1080 30fps'', ''PDF print-ready CMYK'', ''HTML5 300x250''). Ensures deliverable meets technical specifications.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.internal_approval_status IS 'Internal agency approval status before client submission. Ensures quality control and brand compliance before external delivery.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.is_billable IS 'Indicates whether this deliverable is billable to the client or is part of non-billable agency overhead or pro-bono work.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.planned_delivery_date IS 'Target date by which the deliverable is scheduled to be completed and delivered to the client or internal stakeholder.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.priority IS 'Business priority level assigned to this deliverable. Drives resource allocation and scheduling decisions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.rejection_reason IS 'Explanation provided when a deliverable is rejected by client or internal reviewer. Captures feedback for rework and process improvement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.review_round_count IS 'Number of review cycles the deliverable has undergone. Tracks iteration intensity and helps identify scope creep or unclear requirements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.source_system_deliverable_code IS 'Original identifier from the source project management or work management system (e.g., Workfront task ID, Monday.com item ID).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.source_system_name IS 'Name of the operational system from which this deliverable tracking record originated (e.g., ''Workfront'', ''Monday.com'', ''Asana'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.version_number IS 'Version identifier for the deliverable (e.g., ''v1.0'', ''v2.3'', ''Final''). Tracks iteration history and ensures version control.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.deliverable_tracker.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE project.task IS 'Atomic unit of work assigned to an individual or team within a work package. Captures task name, description, task type (creative production, copy writing, media trafficking, client review, QA, approval, etc.), assigned worker reference, assigned team, planned start date, planned end date, actual start date, actual end date, estimated hours, logged hours, completion percentage, priority, status (not started, in progress, blocked, complete), dependency type, predecessor task reference, and source system task ID from Workfront or Monday.com. The operational heartbeat of project execution tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.task_id IS 'Unique identifier for the task. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Tasks need cost center tracking for time-based costing and departmental charge-back. Critical for labor cost allocation when time entries roll up to tasks for financial posting. LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.initiative_id IS 'Reference to the project this task belongs to.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.parent_task_id IS 'Self-referencing FK on task (parent_task_id)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.primary_predecessor_task_id IS 'Reference to the task that must be completed or started before this task can proceed, based on the dependency type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.work_package_id IS 'Reference to the parent work package that contains this task.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.actual_end_date IS 'The actual date when this task was completed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.actual_start_date IS 'The actual date when work on this task began.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.approval_status IS 'The current approval status of the task deliverable (not submitted, pending, approved, rejected, changes requested).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.blocked_reason IS 'Description of the reason why this task is blocked or cannot proceed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.completed_timestamp IS 'The date and time when this task was marked as complete.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.completion_percentage IS 'The percentage of work completed for this task, expressed as a value between 0 and 100.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.deliverable_type IS 'The type of deliverable or output expected from this task (e.g., creative asset, media plan, trafficking sheet, approval document).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.dependency_type IS 'The type of dependency relationship this task has with its predecessor (finish-to-start, start-to-start, finish-to-finish, start-to-finish, or none).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.estimated_hours IS 'The estimated number of hours required to complete this task.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.is_billable IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether the hours logged on this task are billable to the client.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.is_milestone IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether this task represents a project milestone.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.logged_hours IS 'The actual number of hours logged or worked on this task.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.notes IS 'Additional notes, comments, or instructions related to this task.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.planned_end_date IS 'The scheduled date when this task is planned to be completed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.planned_start_date IS 'The scheduled date when work on this task is planned to begin.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.priority IS 'The priority level assigned to this task indicating its relative importance and urgency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.source_system_name IS 'The name of the operational system of record from which this task was sourced (e.g., Workfront, Monday.com).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.source_system_task_code IS 'The unique identifier for this task in the source system (Workfront or Monday.com).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.task_description IS 'Detailed description of the work to be performed in this task.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.task_name IS 'The name or title of the task.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.task_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the task (not started, in progress, blocked, complete, cancelled, on hold).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.task_type IS 'The category or type of work this task represents (e.g., creative production, copywriting, media trafficking, client review, quality assurance, approval).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.task.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE project.time_entry IS 'Individual time entry record submitted by agency staff against a specific project task or work package — the granular time-tracking record at the project level. Captures worker reference, project reference, work package reference, task reference, entry date, hours logged, activity type (creative development, strategy, client management, production, media planning, QA, admin), billable flag, billing rate, billable amount, approval status (submitted, approved, rejected), approver, and source system (Workfront/Monday.com timelog ID). Distinct from talent.timesheet (the aggregated pay-period timesheet header) — this is the line-level project time allocation record.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.time_entry_id IS 'Unique identifier for the time entry record. Primary key for the time entry entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.adjusted_time_entry_id IS 'Self-referencing FK on time_entry (adjusted_time_entry_id)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.assignment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.assignment. Business justification: Time entries are submitted by workers who operate under specific project assignments. Linking time_entry to project_assignment provides the assignment context (billing_rate, cost_rate, assignment_role';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.contract_rate_card_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_rate_card. Business justification: time_entry has billing_rate and cost_rate that must reconcile against the contracted rate card. Advertising agencies bill time against client-negotiated rate cards. This link enables billing validatio LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_rate_card.contract_rate_card_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Time entries must post to cost centers for labor cost allocation, utilization reporting, and departmental P&L. Core requirement for agency financial systems integrating time tracking with GL posting. LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.finance_budget_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.finance_budget. Business justification: Time entries (labor costs) must be charged against the approved finance budget for labor cost tracking and budget consumption reporting. This is core agency resource management — time entries drive bu LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.finance_budget.finance_budget_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.gl_account_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.gl_account. Business justification: Time entries require GL account assignment for payroll expense posting and revenue recognition. Essential for labor cost capitalization, WIP accounting, and financial statement preparation in agency o LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.gl_account.gl_account_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.initiative_id IS 'Reference to the project against which this time was logged. Links to the project domain project entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.rate_card_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.rate_card_line. Business justification: Time entries in advertising are billed at specific rate card line rates by role and service type. rate_card_line has unit_rate, role_title, service_type matching time_entry billing attributes. This li LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.rate_card_line.rate_card_line_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: Time is billed against SOWs. Agencies track SOW-level time for client invoicing, utilization reporting, and validating labor charges against SOW rate cards and authorized budget caps. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sow.sow_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.task_id IS 'Reference to the specific task or deliverable against which time was logged. Links to the project.task entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.work_package_id IS 'Reference to the work package within the project. Represents a logical grouping of tasks for billing or resource planning purposes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.activity_type IS 'The type of work activity performed during this time entry. Categorizes time for resource utilization analysis and billing purposes. Code set: ref.activity_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.approval_status IS 'Current approval state of the time entry. Tracks the workflow from submission through manager approval for payroll and billing processing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.approval_timestamp IS 'The date and time when the time entry was approved or rejected by the approver. Null if not yet reviewed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.billable_amount IS 'The total billable amount for this time entry, calculated as hours_logged multiplied by billing_rate. Null for non-billable entries. Used for revenue recognition and client invoicing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.billing_rate IS 'The hourly billing rate applied to this time entry for client invoicing. May vary by worker role, project contract terms, or activity type. Null for non-billable entries.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.cost_amount IS 'The total internal cost for this time entry, calculated as hours_logged multiplied by cost_rate. Used for project margin analysis and financial reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.cost_rate IS 'The internal cost rate per hour for this worker. Used for project profitability analysis and resource cost tracking. Distinct from billing_rate.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for the billable amount (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP). Supports multi-currency project billing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.entry_date IS 'The calendar date on which the work was performed. Used for timesheet aggregation and project timeline tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.hours_logged IS 'The number of hours worked on this task for the entry date. Supports fractional hours (e.g., 1.5 hours, 0.25 hours).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.is_billable IS 'Indicates whether this time entry is billable to the client. True for billable time, False for non-billable or internal time.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.is_locked IS 'Indicates whether this time entry is locked and cannot be edited. True when the entry has been processed for payroll or billing. False for editable entries.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.is_overtime IS 'Indicates whether this time entry represents overtime hours. True for overtime, False for regular hours. Used for payroll processing and labor cost analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.location IS 'The physical or virtual location where the work was performed. Used for resource allocation analysis and compliance with remote work policies.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.notes IS 'Optional free-text notes or comments provided by the worker describing the work performed. Used for detailed activity tracking and client reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.rejection_reason IS 'Free-text explanation provided by the approver when rejecting a time entry. Null for approved or pending entries.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.source_system_code IS 'The unique identifier for this time entry in the source system (Workfront or Monday.com). Used for data lineage and reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.source_system_name IS 'The name of the system from which this time entry was ingested. Supports multi-system time tracking integration.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.submitted_timestamp IS 'The date and time when the worker submitted this time entry for approval. Null for draft entries.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.time_entry.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE project.initiative IS 'Master record for an agency project or engagement — the authoritative SSOT for project identity, scope, and lifecycle within the agency. Captures project name, type (campaign production, brand strategy, media planning, PR activation, etc.), status (briefing, planning, in-flight, on-hold, completed, cancelled), priority, start and end dates, planned vs. actual duration, client account reference, associated campaign reference, owning department, project manager, delivery methodology (agile, waterfall, hybrid), source system (Workfront/Monday.com) project ID, and overall health indicator. Serves as the top-level container for all work breakdown structures, tasks, milestones, and resource assignments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.initiative_id IS 'Unique identifier for the agency project or engagement. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the client advertiser account for whom this project is being executed. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.advertiser.advertiser_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.agency_relationship_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.agency_relationship. Business justification: Projects are delivered under specific agency relationship agreements (AOR, project-based retainer, pitch work). Tracking which relationship governs the work is essential for billing rules, scope bound LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.agency_relationship.agency_relationship_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.agreement_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.agreement. Business justification: Master agreements govern multi-project client relationships. Agencies link initiatives to MSAs to apply correct rate cards, enforce compliance obligations, and manage multi-year retainer terms across LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.agreement.agreement_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.attribution_model_id IS 'Foreign key linking to performance.attribution_model. Business justification: Strategic initiatives define attribution methodology for performance evaluation. Real business process: campaign planning phase where strategists select attribution model (last-click, linear, data-dri LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.attribution_model.attribution_model_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: Initiatives are executed on behalf of a specific brand. Brand-level reporting — SOV tracking, brand health metrics, budget utilization by brand — requires linking initiatives to client_brand. initiati LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.brand.brand_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the associated marketing campaign if this project is part of a broader campaign initiative. Nullable for non-campaign projects. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Projects must be assigned to cost centers for financial reporting, budget allocation, and P&L tracking in agency operations. Essential for departmental profitability analysis and overhead allocation. LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.parent_initiative_id IS 'Self-referencing FK on initiative (parent_initiative_id)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: Initiatives execute SOW-defined scope. Agencies track SOW-to-project mapping for revenue recognition, deliverable tracking, budget burn analysis, and client invoicing against contractual commitments. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sow.sow_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Projects/initiatives frequently engage vendors for media buying, tech platforms, creative production. Tracking primary supplier enables project vendor management, cost allocation, and vendor performan LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.actual_cost IS 'Total actual cost incurred to date for labor, materials, and external expenses. Updated as costs are recorded.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.actual_duration_days IS 'Actual elapsed duration of the project in calendar days. Populated upon project completion.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.billing_type IS 'Commercial model under which the project is billed to the client.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.budget_amount IS 'Total approved budget allocated for this project in the agency''s reporting currency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.budget_currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for the project budget (e.g., USD, GBP, EUR).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.cancellation_date IS 'Date when the project was formally cancelled. Populated only for cancelled projects.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.cancellation_reason IS 'Explanation for why the project was cancelled (e.g., client budget cuts, scope changes, strategic pivot).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.client_satisfaction_score IS 'Client-reported satisfaction rating for the project, typically on a scale of 1.00 to 5.00. Captured post-delivery or at milestones.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.completion_date IS 'Actual date when all project deliverables were completed and accepted by the client.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.deliverables_summary IS 'High-level summary of key deliverables expected from this project (e.g., creative assets, media plans, campaign reports).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.delivery_methodology IS 'Project management methodology applied for planning and execution (e.g., agile sprints, waterfall phases, hybrid approach).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.end_date IS 'Planned or actual date when project work is scheduled to complete or was completed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.health_indicator IS 'Overall health status of the project based on schedule, budget, scope, and quality metrics. Green indicates on-track, yellow indicates at-risk, red indicates critical issues.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.initiative_name IS 'Human-readable name of the project or engagement, used for identification and reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.initiative_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the project indicating its stage in the execution workflow.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.is_billable IS 'Indicates whether this project is billable to the client (true) or internal/non-billable (false).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.is_confidential IS 'Indicates whether this project is subject to confidentiality or non-disclosure agreements requiring restricted access.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.kickoff_date IS 'Date of the formal project kickoff meeting with the client and internal team.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.notes IS 'Free-form notes capturing additional context, special instructions, or important observations about the project.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.owning_department IS 'Primary agency department responsible for delivering this project. Code set: ref.owning_department.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.planned_duration_days IS 'Originally estimated duration of the project in calendar days from start to end.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.priority IS 'Business priority level assigned to the project for resource allocation and scheduling decisions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.project_code IS 'Externally-known unique alphanumeric code assigned to the project for client communication and billing. Typically follows agency naming convention.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.project_type IS 'Classification of the project based on the primary service offering or deliverable type. Code set: ref.project_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.risk_level IS 'Overall risk assessment for the project based on complexity, dependencies, client volatility, and resource constraints.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.scope_description IS 'Detailed narrative describing the project scope, objectives, deliverables, and boundaries.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.source_system_code IS 'Unique project identifier from the originating system of record (Workfront, Monday.com, or other project management platform).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.source_system_name IS 'Name of the project management system from which this project record was ingested.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.start_date IS 'Planned or actual date when project work officially begins.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.initiative.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE project.milestone IS 'Significant scheduled checkpoint or deliverable gate within a project lifecycle. Captures milestone name, description, milestone type (kickoff, creative review, client approval, campaign launch, post-campaign report, billing trigger, contractual gate), planned date, actual date, status (upcoming, achieved, missed, deferred), owner, associated work package, linked SOW contractual milestone reference, and variance in days between planned and actual achievement. Used for client reporting, billing triggers, and executive project health dashboards.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.milestone_id IS 'Unique identifier for the project milestone. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.amendment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.amendment. Business justification: Contract amendments in advertising frequently revise milestone dates and deliverable scope. Linking project_milestone.amendment_id → amendment provides the audit trail showing which amendment triggere LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.amendment.amendment_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.initiative_id IS 'Reference to the parent project to which this milestone belongs.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.replanned_from_project_milestone_id IS 'Self-referencing FK on project_milestone (replanned_from_project_milestone_id)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.sla_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sla. Business justification: Contractual milestone gates in advertising are governed by SLAs (e.g., creative delivery turnaround SLAs). project_milestone.is_contractual_gate flag signals this need. Linking to sla enables SLA brea LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sla.sla_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Contractual campaign milestones (e.g., creative delivery gate, campaign launch) are often vendor-dependent in advertising. Linking supplier_id to project_milestone enables vendor-specific milestone tr LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.work_package_id IS 'Reference to the associated work package or phase within the project structure.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.acceptance_criteria IS 'Specific, measurable criteria that must be met for the milestone to be considered successfully achieved and approved by stakeholders.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.actual_date IS 'Actual date the milestone was achieved or completed. Null if milestone has not yet been reached.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.approved_timestamp IS 'Timestamp when the milestone completion was formally approved by the designated approver. Null if not yet approved.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.baseline_date IS 'Baseline date captured at project approval or contract signature, used for variance analysis and performance measurement against original commitment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.completion_percentage IS 'Percentage of work completed toward achieving this milestone, expressed as a decimal (0.00 to 100.00). Used for progress tracking and earned value analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.deliverable_description IS 'Detailed description of the tangible deliverable or output associated with this milestone (e.g., ''Final creative assets in all formats'', ''Campaign performance dashboard'', ''Client presentation deck'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.dependency_count IS 'Number of predecessor tasks or milestones that must be completed before this milestone can be achieved. Used for dependency analysis and scheduling.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.forecast_date IS 'Current forecasted date for milestone completion based on project progress and risk assessment. Updated regularly during project execution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.is_billing_trigger IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether achievement of this milestone triggers invoice generation or payment milestone per the client contract.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.is_contractual_gate IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether this milestone is a contractually binding checkpoint defined in the SOW, requiring formal client sign-off before proceeding.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.is_critical_path IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether this milestone lies on the project critical path. Delays to critical path milestones directly impact overall project completion date.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.milestone_description IS 'Detailed description of the milestone deliverable, acceptance criteria, and business significance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.milestone_name IS 'Business-friendly name of the milestone (e.g., ''Creative Concept Approval'', ''Campaign Launch'', ''Post-Campaign Report Delivery'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.milestone_type IS 'Classification of the milestone by its business function: kickoff (project initiation), creative_review (internal creative approval), client_approval (client sign-off gate), campaign_launch (media go-live), post_campaign_report (campaign performance delivery), billing_trigger (invoice generation event), contractual_gate (SOW-defined checkpoint). Code set: ref.milestone_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.notes IS 'Free-text field for additional context, issues, decisions, or stakeholder feedback related to the milestone.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.planned_date IS 'Originally scheduled date for milestone achievement as defined in the project plan or SOW.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.project_milestone_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the milestone: upcoming (not yet started), in_progress (work underway toward milestone), achieved (successfully completed on or before planned date), missed (completed after planned date or not completed by deadline), deferred (postponed to future date), cancelled (no longer required).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.risk_level IS 'Current risk assessment for on-time milestone achievement: low (on track, no issues), medium (minor concerns, monitoring required), high (significant risk of delay), critical (delay imminent or already occurred).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.sow_milestone_reference IS 'External reference code linking this milestone to a contractual milestone defined in the client Statement of Work (SOW). Used for contractual compliance and billing trigger validation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.variance_days IS 'Calculated variance in days between planned date and actual date. Positive values indicate delay (missed deadline), negative values indicate early completion. Null if milestone not yet achieved.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.milestone.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE project.project_brief IS 'Internal project initiation brief that translates a client brief or SOW into an actionable agency project plan. Captures brief title, project type, originating client brief reference, associated campaign reference, strategic objectives, target audience summary, key deliverables list, channel mix, budget envelope, timeline constraints, success criteria, key stakeholders, creative direction notes, and brief status (draft, approved, in-execution). Distinct from client.client_brief (client-submitted) and creative.creative_brief (creative-specific) — this is the project management layer brief governing overall project execution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.project_brief_id IS 'Unique identifier for the project brief record. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the client advertiser for whom this project is being executed. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.advertiser.advertiser_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: Project briefs are scoped to a specific client brand (e.g., Nike Running vs. Nike Basketball), driving brand safety rules, creative direction, and brand-level budget allocation. Advertising PMs always LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.brand.brand_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the associated campaign that this project brief supports. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.client_brief_id IS 'Reference to the originating client brief that this project brief translates into an actionable plan. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.client_brief.client_brief_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.initiative_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.initiative. Business justification: project_brief translates client briefs into actionable agency projects but currently has no direct link to the initiative product that represents the project execution. Adding initiative_id creates th';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.segment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.segment. Business justification: Project briefs specify primary target audience segments for campaign planning and creative development. Agencies link briefs to segments to ensure creative deliverables align with audience strategy an LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.segment.segment_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: Project briefs operationalize SOW commitments. Agencies must track which SOW funds each brief to validate scope, budget authority, and deliverable alignment during project kickoff and execution. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sow.sow_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.superseded_project_brief_id IS 'Self-referencing FK on project_brief (superseded_project_brief_id)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.target_persona_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.persona. Business justification: Project briefs reference target personas to guide strategic planning and creative direction. Agencies link briefs to personas to ensure all project deliverables (creative, media, messaging) align with LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.persona.persona_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.approved_by IS 'Name or identifier of the individual who approved the project brief for execution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.approved_date IS 'Date when the project brief was formally approved for execution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.brand_safety_notes IS 'Brand safety considerations, content adjacency guidelines, and risk mitigation measures for media placement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.brief_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the project brief indicating its stage in the approval and execution workflow.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.budget_currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for the budget envelope amount.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.budget_envelope_amount IS 'Total budget allocation or envelope amount approved for this project execution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.channel_mix IS 'Description of the media and marketing channels to be utilized in this project (e.g., digital, TV, OOH, social, CTV).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.completion_timestamp IS 'Timestamp when the project was marked as completed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.compliance_requirements IS 'Regulatory, legal, and compliance requirements applicable to this project (e.g., GDPR, CCPA, FTC guidelines, ASA standards).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.creative_direction_notes IS 'High-level creative direction, brand guidelines, tone, messaging themes, and creative considerations for the project.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.execution_start_timestamp IS 'Timestamp when project execution officially began following brief approval.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.is_active IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether the project brief is currently active and in use.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.key_deliverables IS 'Comprehensive list of key deliverables, outputs, and work products expected from this project.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.key_stakeholders IS 'List of key stakeholders, decision-makers, and approvers involved in this project from both agency and client sides.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.measurement_framework IS 'Description of the measurement and analytics framework to be used for tracking project performance and outcomes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.planned_end_date IS 'Planned completion date for project execution as defined in the project brief.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.planned_start_date IS 'Planned start date for project execution as defined in the project brief.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.priority_level IS 'Priority classification of the project brief indicating urgency and resource allocation priority.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.project_type IS 'Classification of the project type indicating the nature of work to be performed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.risk_considerations IS 'Identified risks, dependencies, and mitigation strategies relevant to project execution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.scope_description IS 'Detailed description of the project scope, including in-scope and out-of-scope activities.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.strategic_objectives IS 'High-level strategic goals and business objectives that this project aims to achieve for the client.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.submitted_timestamp IS 'Timestamp when the project brief was submitted for approval.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.success_criteria IS 'Defined success criteria and key performance indicators (KPIs) that will be used to measure project success.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.target_audience_summary IS 'Summary description of the target audience demographics, psychographics, and behavioral characteristics for this project.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.timeline_constraints IS 'Description of any timeline constraints, critical milestones, or deadline dependencies that impact project scheduling.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.title IS 'The descriptive title of the project brief that summarizes the project scope.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_brief.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE project.project_budget IS 'Project-level budget record defining the approved financial envelope for a project, distinct from finance.budget (which operates at cost center and campaign level). Captures project reference, budget version, budget type (original approved, revised, client-approved), total approved budget, budget by phase or work package, contingency reserve, management reserve, currency, approval date, approver, budget status (draft, approved, locked, over-budget), total committed spend, total actual spend, and remaining budget. Enables project financial control and client billing reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.project_budget_id IS 'Unique identifier for the project budget record. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.amendment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.amendment. Business justification: Contract amendments in advertising trigger project budget revisions (scope changes, budget increases). Linking project_budget.amendment_id → amendment provides the audit trail showing which amendment LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.amendment.amendment_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: Agency project budgets are allocated and tracked at brand level for brand-level P&L and budget utilization reporting. Finance teams require direct brand attribution on project budgets to produce brand LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.brand.brand_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.contract_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_insertion_order. Business justification: In advertising agencies, project budgets are built directly against Insertion Orders — the IO is the spend authorization document. This link enables IO-to-budget reconciliation reporting, a core finan LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_insertion_order.contract_insertion_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Project budgets are posted to cost centers for management accounting and overhead allocation. project_budget has a denormalized cost_center_code plain attribute but no FK. Linking to cost_center enabl LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.finance_budget_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.finance_budget. Business justification: Agency project budgets must reconcile against the finance-controlled finance_budget for variance reporting, SOX compliance, and budget approval workflows. Finance teams need to trace project spend bac LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.finance_budget.finance_budget_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.gl_account_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.gl_account. Business justification: Project budgets need GL account mapping for financial statement integration, accrual posting, and revenue/expense classification. Required for month-end close and financial reporting in agency ERP sys LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.gl_account.gl_account_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.initiative_id IS 'Reference to the parent project for which this budget is defined. Links to the project master record.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.plan_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.plan. Business justification: Project budgets allocate funds to specific media plans. Required for variance analysis between planned media spend and project budget, enabling financial forecasting, budget reallocation decisions, an LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.plan.plan_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.revised_from_project_budget_id IS 'Self-referencing FK on project_budget (revised_from_project_budget_id)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: Project budgets are allocated from SOW budgets. Finance tracks SOW-to-project budget mapping for billing reconciliation, variance analysis, and ensuring project spend does not exceed contractual autho LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sow.sow_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: project_budget contains a `third_party_vendor_budget` attribute, confirming per-vendor budget allocation is tracked. Linking supplier_id enables budget-vs-actual spend reporting by vendor — a standard LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.vendor_rate_card_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.vendor_rate_card. Business justification: In advertising, project budgets for media and production are built from vendor rate cards. Linking vendor_rate_card_id to project_budget enables budget-to-rate-card traceability — auditors and finance LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.vendor_rate_card.vendor_rate_card_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.work_package_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.work_package. Business justification: project_budget currently carries work_breakdown_structure_code as a free-text string reference to the WBS. Adding a proper FK work_package_id to project.work_package normalizes this relationship, repl';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.approval_date IS 'Date on which this budget version was formally approved by the authorized approver or governance body.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.approved_timestamp IS 'Timestamp when this budget version was formally approved. Captures the precise moment of approval for audit and compliance purposes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.baseline_budget_flag IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether this budget version represents the original approved baseline for the project. True for the baseline version, False for revisions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.budget_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the budget: draft (in preparation), submitted (pending approval), approved (active), locked (no further changes), over-budget (exceeded threshold), or closed (project complete).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.budget_type IS 'Classification of the budget record: original approved (baseline), revised (internal adjustment), client-approved (client sign-off), internal forecast (planning estimate), or contingency (reserve allocation).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.client_approval_date IS 'Date on which the client formally approved this budget version. Null if not yet client-approved.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.client_approved_flag IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether this budget version has been formally approved by the client. True if client-approved, False otherwise.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.contingency_reserve IS 'Budget reserve allocated for identified risks and known-unknowns. Typically controlled by the project manager and released as needed for scope changes or risk mitigation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.creative_production_budget IS 'Portion of the total budget allocated to creative development and production activities, including design, video production, photography, and Digital Asset Management (DAM).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for all monetary amounts in this budget (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.effective_end_date IS 'Date on which this budget version ceases to be effective. Null for the current active budget version.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.effective_start_date IS 'Date from which this budget version becomes effective and active for financial tracking and control.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.fiscal_quarter IS 'Fiscal quarter to which this project budget primarily applies (Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4). Supports quarterly financial planning and Quarterly Business Review (QBR) processes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.fiscal_year IS 'Fiscal year to which this project budget applies (e.g., 2024, 2025). Enables financial period alignment and year-over-year analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.labor_budget IS 'Portion of the total budget allocated to labor costs, including salaries, contractor fees, and Full-Time Equivalent (FTE) resources.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.locked_timestamp IS 'Timestamp when this budget version was locked to prevent further modifications. Null if the budget is still open for changes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.management_reserve IS 'Budget reserve allocated for unknown-unknowns and unplanned scope changes. Typically controlled by senior management and requires formal approval to access.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.media_budget IS 'Portion of the total budget allocated to media buying and placement costs across all channels (digital, broadcast, print, Out-of-Home (OOH), etc.).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.notes IS 'Free-text field for additional notes, assumptions, constraints, or context related to this budget version. Supports audit trail and knowledge transfer.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.remaining_budget IS 'Calculated remaining budget available for allocation. Typically total_approved_budget minus (total_committed_spend + total_actual_spend).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.revision_reason IS 'Textual explanation of why this budget version was revised from the previous version. Captures scope changes, client requests, cost overruns, or other justifications.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.source_system_budget_code IS 'Original budget identifier from the source system (e.g., Workfront project budget ID, SAP Project Systems (PS) budget ID). Enables traceability and reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.source_system_name IS 'Name of the operational system from which this budget record originated (e.g., Workfront, SAP S/4HANA PS, Mediaocean Prisma). Supports data lineage and Extract Transform Load (ETL) auditing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.technology_budget IS 'Portion of the total budget allocated to technology costs, including ad serving platforms, Demand-Side Platform (DSP), Data Management Platform (DMP), analytics tools, and Application Programming Interface (API) integrations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.third_party_vendor_budget IS 'Portion of the total budget allocated to external vendor services, including research firms, data providers, freelancers, and specialized consultants.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.total_actual_spend IS 'Cumulative amount of budget that has been actually spent (invoiced and paid or accrued) against this project budget.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.total_approved_budget IS 'The total financial envelope approved for this project budget version. Represents the authorized spending limit.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.total_committed_spend IS 'Cumulative amount of budget that has been committed through Purchase Orders (PO), Insertion Orders (IO), contracts, or other binding commitments, but not yet invoiced or paid.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.utilization_percentage IS 'Percentage of the total approved budget that has been utilized (committed or spent). Calculated as ((total_committed_spend + total_actual_spend) / total_approved_budget) * 100.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.version IS 'Version identifier for this budget iteration (e.g., v1.0, v2.1, 2024-Q1-Rev3). Enables tracking of budget revisions over the project lifecycle.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.project_budget.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE project.resource_plan IS 'Forward-looking resource demand plan for a project, capturing the planned allocation of agency talent and capacity across the project timeline. Stores project reference, planning period (week, sprint, month), role or discipline required, planned FTE count, planned hours, skill requirements, seniority level, department, cost rate applied, total planned cost, and plan version. Distinct from talent.resource_allocation (which records confirmed individual assignments) — this is the demand-side capacity plan used for staffing decisions and capacity forecasting at the project level.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.resource_plan_id IS 'Unique identifier for the resource plan record. Primary key for the resource plan entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.contract_rate_card_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_rate_card. Business justification: Agency resource plans are costed against negotiated rate cards. resource_plan has cost_rate, role_code, seniority_level that must align with contracted rates. This link enables accurate cost planning LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_rate_card.contract_rate_card_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.initiative_id IS 'Reference to the project for which this resource plan is created. Links to the project master entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.revised_from_resource_plan_id IS 'Self-referencing FK on resource_plan (revised_from_resource_plan_id)';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.work_package_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.work_package. Business justification: Resource plans are scoped not only at the initiative level but also at the work package (WBS node) level — e.g., ''we need 2 senior copywriters for the Creative Production work package.'' Adding work_pa';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.allocation_priority IS 'The priority level for securing this resource allocation (critical, high, medium, low), used for capacity planning and resource conflict resolution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.approval_date IS 'The date when this resource plan was approved by the project manager or resource manager.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.approved_by IS 'The name or identifier of the person who approved this resource plan.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.billable_flag IS 'Indicates whether the planned hours for this resource are billable to the client (True) or non-billable/internal (False).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.cost_rate IS 'The internal cost rate applied per hour or per FTE for this role, used for capacity planning and project costing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.cost_rate_currency IS 'The three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for the cost rate (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.department_code IS 'The code representing the department or cost center responsible for this resource allocation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.department_name IS 'The name of the department or cost center responsible for this resource allocation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.discipline IS 'The broad functional discipline or department to which the role belongs (creative, strategy, media, account management, production, analytics, technology, operations). Code set: ref.discipline.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.location_preference IS 'The preferred work location for this resource allocation (onsite, remote, hybrid, or any).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.notes IS 'Free-text notes or comments about this resource plan, including special requirements, constraints, or assumptions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.office_location IS 'The specific office or geographic location from which the resource is expected to work (e.g., New York, London, Remote).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.plan_status IS 'The current lifecycle status of the resource plan (draft, submitted for approval, approved, active, superseded by newer version, or cancelled).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.plan_version IS 'Version identifier for the resource plan, enabling tracking of plan iterations and revisions over time (e.g., v1.0, v2.1, draft, final).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.planned_fte IS 'The planned Full-Time Equivalent (FTE) allocation for this role during the planning period. 1.0 represents one full-time resource; 0.5 represents half-time allocation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.planned_hours IS 'The total number of hours planned for this role during the planning period.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.planning_period_end_date IS 'The end date of the planning period for which resources are being planned.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.planning_period_start_date IS 'The start date of the planning period for which resources are being planned.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.planning_period_type IS 'The time granularity used for resource planning (week, sprint, month, quarter, or project phase).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.role_code IS 'The standardized code representing the role or discipline required for this resource plan (e.g., ACD for Art Creative Director, CPY for Copywriter, STR for Strategist).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.role_name IS 'The human-readable name of the role or discipline required (e.g., Art Director, Copywriter, Media Planner, Account Executive).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.seniority_level IS 'The seniority or experience level required for the role (junior, mid-level, senior, lead, principal, director).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.skill_requirements IS 'Specific skills, competencies, or certifications required for the role (e.g., Adobe Creative Suite, Google Ads Certification, Salesforce CRM, Spanish language fluency).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.total_planned_cost IS 'The total planned cost for this resource allocation, calculated as planned hours multiplied by cost rate.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.resource_plan.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_by.';

COMMENT ON TABLE project.work_package IS 'Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) node representing a discrete, manageable unit of work within a project. Captures WBS code, package name, description, parent package reference (enabling hierarchical decomposition), level in the WBS hierarchy, owning discipline or department (creative, media, strategy, production, PR), planned effort hours, actual effort hours, planned cost, actual cost, status, and completion percentage. Enables multi-level decomposition of project scope into deliverable-oriented components aligned to Workfront/Monday.com task groups.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.work_package_id IS 'Unique identifier for the work package within the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS). Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Work packages require cost center assignment for labor cost allocation and profitability analysis by discipline. Enables accurate project costing and departmental charge-back in agency financial syste LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.initiative_id IS 'Reference to the parent project or campaign engagement that this work package belongs to.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.parent_work_package_id IS 'Reference to the parent work package in the hierarchical WBS structure. Null for top-level packages.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.segment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.segment. Business justification: Advertising work packages are scoped to specific audience segments (e.g., ''Build Retargeting Segment'', ''Activate Prospecting Audience''). Project managers need this link to track segment-specific work LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.segment.segment_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: Work packages decompose SOW scope. Agencies map WBS elements to SOW scope items for traceability, ensuring all contracted deliverables are planned and no out-of-scope work is executed without authoriz LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sow.sow_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: In advertising operations, specific work packages (e.g., creative production, media buying execution) are assigned to external vendors. Linking supplier_id to work_package enables vendor accountabilit LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.actual_cost IS 'Actual cost incurred for this work package to date. Used for cost variance analysis and Earned Value Management (EVM).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.actual_effort_hours IS 'Actual labor hours expended on this work package to date. Tracked from time entry systems for variance analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.actual_end_date IS 'Actual date when work on this package was completed. Null if not yet completed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.actual_start_date IS 'Actual date when work on this package commenced. Null if not yet started.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.approval_status IS 'Current approval state of the work package deliverable. Tracks client or internal stakeholder sign-off.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.approved_by IS 'Name or identifier of the person who approved this work package. Null if not yet approved.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.approved_date IS 'Date when this work package was formally approved. Null if not yet approved.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.completion_percentage IS 'Percentage of work completed for this package (0.00 to 100.00). Used for progress tracking and Earned Value (EV) calculation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for planned and actual cost amounts (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.deliverable_type IS 'Classification of the primary deliverable produced by this work package (e.g., ''Creative Brief'', ''Media Plan'', ''Campaign Report'', ''Video Asset''). Code set: ref.deliverable_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.discipline IS 'Primary agency discipline or department responsible for executing this work package (e.g., creative, media, strategy, production, PR). Code set: ref.discipline.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.is_billable IS 'Indicates whether this work package is billable to the client (true) or non-billable internal work (false).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.is_critical_path IS 'Indicates whether this work package is on the project critical path. Delays to critical path items directly impact project completion date.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.notes IS 'Free-form text field for additional context, instructions, risks, or issues related to this work package.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.planned_cost IS 'Budgeted cost for this work package including labor, materials, and other direct costs. Baseline for Earned Value Management (EVM).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.planned_effort_hours IS 'Estimated total labor hours required to complete this work package. Used for resource capacity planning and baseline cost estimation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.planned_end_date IS 'Scheduled date when work on this package is planned to be completed. Used for baseline schedule tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.planned_start_date IS 'Scheduled date when work on this package is planned to begin. Used for baseline schedule tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.priority IS 'Business priority level assigned to this work package for resource allocation and scheduling decisions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.wbs_code IS 'Hierarchical alphanumeric code representing the work package position in the WBS (e.g., 1.2.3.1). Enables structured decomposition and rollup reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.wbs_level IS 'Numeric depth of this work package in the WBS hierarchy (1 = top level, 2 = second level, etc.). Enables level-based filtering and rollup.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.work_package_description IS 'Detailed narrative describing the scope, deliverables, and objectives of this work package. Provides context for resource planning and execution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.work_package_name IS 'Short, descriptive name of the work package that clearly identifies the deliverable or work scope (e.g., ''Creative Concept Development'', ''Media Buy Execution'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.work_package_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the work package indicating progress and execution state.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.work_package_type IS 'Classification of the work package within the WBS structure (deliverable-oriented, milestone, phase, task group, or control account).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN project.work_package.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';
